rsh and rshd are very, very sick under AIX.  It doesn't help that
the r-commands are Bezerkely inventions; all Unices have weird and
misdesigned behaviour and little to no specification.  Consider
the way that host names are matched, for example, and the fact
that there is no logging.

But AIX's versions are unlike any others I have seen before (and
I have a fairly wide experience) and even worse documented.  I
have got IBM to 'fix' one bug by documenting it, but can't face
the effort of even reporting most of the gotchas.  IBM have
refused to provide me with a specification.

Given that you are referring to rsh (not rshd), my guess is that
you have been Kerberised - i.e. a basic facility on your system
has been rendered incomprehensibly non-functional by IBM's
Kerberos hooks.  You COULD disable Kerberos, but that is an evil
process and requires secret incantations.

It certainly can be made to work, but is non-trivial.  Sorry I
can't help more.


