Hello,

It seems that with patchkit 7, NHD3 is not needed anymore.
We came accross the same situation and tried to deinstall OSHH*
with no luck.
You're also unable to 'baseline' the system from dupatch.
We then decided to remove all the admin from the NHD3 kit, like
# rm /usr/.smdb./OSHH*
The we baselined the system, and installed patchkit 7.
The only thing we forgot is booting from genvmunix instead of
GENERIC, because we didn't realize that it isn't neccessary
anymore.
Because we forgot to boot genvmunix, we weren't able to recognize
the Oxygen VX1 graphics adapter which we were looking for.

We then decided to go back to v4.0f incl. NHD3 and partially installed 
PK7 for the moment (restored backup).
Later we decided to go for fresh install of V4.0F, forget NHD3 and 
installed PK7. All Ok then.

You may try our first method as well, since I'm pretty sure that it
makes a chance, we just didn't test it enough.

Keep a good backup handy!

regards,
Jelle

