Well, the first place you can look for assigned ports is IANA:

http://www.iana.org/assignments/port-numbers

I'll try and fill-in the blanks the other replies have left:

111 - portmapper, needed if you're doing any RPC services, like NFS

596 - smsd, the SysMan Station daemon

316 - the Java authentication server

49400 - config_hmmod, don't know what this is

49401 - don't have one of those on my system

BTW, there are two ways to cross-reference a port to a pid.

1. Use the kdbx inpcb and socket extentions.

2. Use lsof, it's freely available for download.

-Brian


