>> is there any way to find out what kind of memory boards (32,64 or 128) are
>> installed in Alphaserver 800, we are running "OSF1 V4.0 878 alpha",
>without
>> rebooting the system.

I don't have an AlphaServer 800, to check, but many Alpha systems
generate FRU events when they boot.  FRU being Field Replaceable
Unit.  These are written to the binary event log.  DECevent can
translate them.  I doubt uerf(8) can.  On my Alphaserver 1200,
these FRU events include entries for the DIMM pairs, which includes
how big each one is.  For some total memory capacities and memory
options, the configuration can be derived.

