Hi all,
I am testing a FORTRAN code on 2 CPU Alpha Tru64Unix (OSF1 V5.1 1885
alpha).  The code is parallelised using LAM-MPI.
The job runs as four concurrent processes which communicate with each
other.  When the job is started, all four processes attempt to read four
respective files from the same file server (in this case, the local hard
disk) and the processes halt during I/O process.

In order to fix this problem, I ran dxkerneltuner and modified the value
of vm_ubcdirtypercent from 40 to 10, as recommended by syscheck to
prevent the so-called I/O flooding.  vm-page-free-target was also
modified from 1024 to 1536, also recommended by syscheck.  The I/O
problem hasn't been solved completely but it seems to get better as the
error occurs later in the program execution.

The error message is as follows:
forrtl: severe (22): input record too long, unit 2, file ...

So, I think further tuning may be necessary to get the program to
function correctly.  Does anybody have any ideas/recommendations?

Michael

PS. This posting is related to the previous posting called "compaq
fortran limits".



