I expericenced similar problem like that before.
I couldn't even send out mails with "-r" option.
I found out that the external receiving server was setup to reverse 
checking of my local workstation fully qualified name (hostname + domainname).
I have a non-fully qualified name so the mails were rejected at that end.
I tried and it worked with Hotmail. Seem that Hotmail doesn't care (no wonder
spams get to Hotmail a lot).
You can try see if Hotmail accepted mails sending from your box or not.

For solution, you can either ask the receiving end to modify their settings.
That is very unlikely. Or you can modify your Mail Transport Agent. 
I use sendmail so I modified the "envelope sender rewriting" rules and it works OK
for me.
I can send you the bit I modified in sendmail.cf if you want.
It is on Solaris 8 though. I think it should be very much the same with sendmail
in Tru64.
I am not expert in sendmail so check sendmail web site and its newsgroup,
mailinglist for solution.

