In article <b9019227.0202010628.7f06a60a@posting.google.com>, Narasimha
<mknarasimha@hotmail.com> wrote:

X  Hi,
X  
X  This is regarding the showfile -x M-6 of the M-6 file in the .tags directory:
X  Does the file M-6 alone consist of the extent information for the fileset or
X  do other files also consist of extent Information about the fileset?
X  
X  Thanks,
X  Narasimha.
 
.tags/M-6 is the Bitfile Metadata Table (BMT) of the first volume of
the domain.  ./tags/M-12 is the BMT for the 2nd volume, ./tags/M-18 is
the BMT for the 3rd volume, etc...

The BMT is domain wide and provides metadata storage for _ALL_ filesets
in a domain.  It is not specificily associated with any individual
fileset.

A fileset is a name space.  Its primary component is a tag directory
that contains translations between the bitfile tag ID (like an inode
number) and the file's primary mcell (mcells are stored in the BMT and
a file may use multiple mcells depending on its metadata storage
needs).  There is a tag directory for each fileset in a domain.  The
root tag directory keeps track of each fileset's tag directory.

As to file extent information, yes, that is stored in the BMT's along
with all the other file attribute and metadata information.  A file may
have mcells in multiple which are chained together and may be located
on multiple BMT's.  For example, if a file has storage on 2 volumes of
a domain, then the BMT of each of those volumes will contain mcells for
that file to describe that storage.

                                        Bob Harris
 
