Hi,

There is a system-wide parameter that restricts it so
only root can set the execute bit.  It is in the
vfs subsystem and it is called "noadd_exec_access"
If this is set to 1 no-one on the system other than
root can set the execute bit.

To check this attribute do
   # sysconfig -q vfs
and look for noadd_exec_access.

To change it you have to modify the sysconfigtab and
reboot.  For info on this attribute see "man sys_attrs_vfs"
and look for noadd_exec_access.

This attribute can also be modified via the security
setup GUI, I don't remember where in the process, but
there is a button you can set to set or clear this 
attribute from secconfig.  If this is your problem, 
that's probably how it got set.

Ann


