Yo, after a few weeks of messing around with syslog.conf, I finally
got the SonicWall to accurately remotely log on my Linux machine.  You
are correct that the SW used the local0 facility.  Something I later
found out that you might be interested in is that each
vendor/service/application, when written, can be specified to utilize
local0-local7.  SW, evidentially, either specified local0, or, more
likely, did not specify anything, which then defaulted to local0.

So, you next question regarding multiple devices sending to the 600au
depends on each "item" that will be sending data - did the
app/vendor/service specify a facility, or will they all default to
local0, which could be messy.


