This may not relate to the original question, but if you build
software which uses perl's shared library, then it'll not work 
because under Tru64 5.1 (V5.1 732), they have /usr/lib/perl-5.005/...
while under Tru64 5.1A (V5.1 1885), they changed/upgraded it to
/usr/lib/perl-5.6.0/.... Maybe perl isn't Compaq's, so libperl.so
can't be put in /usr/shlib.

I built vim use perl,

# ldd /usr/local/bin/vim
        Main  =>   /usr/local/bin/vim
	 :
	libperl.so =>
/usr/lib/perl-5.005/lib/5.00503/alpha-dec_osf/CORE/libperl.so
	 :

However, same vim binary can't run under 5.1A because libperl.so
is now in /usr/lib/perl-5.6.0/lib/5.6.0/alpha-dec_osf/CORE. So I 
had to copy /usr/lib/perl-5.005 from a v5.1 machine to v5.1A
machine to make vim work. BTW, we build our own /usr/local on
one machine (v5.1) then rdist to others (mix of v5.1 and v5.1A). 

