Hi Bob,

I thought i had cleared out our goal. Our goal is to find the extents
that a
fileset occupies on disk.People can write scripts read the extent
information(offset and size and perform backups) Currently there is no
way to do this other than walking thro all the files of the fileset
and then finding all the extents occupied by all the files and then
collapse them wherever possible and give the output(this effort is
time consuming). Our goal was to find the extents that a fileset maps
to but since you mentioned that the fileset is just a name in a name
space we probably need to stick to the method you mentioned.
Continuing on the previous conversation: If we indeed walk thro all
the files in the fileset and get the file extents we would need to
find the extents of the special files M-6 and M-12 as well but these
files are somehow hidden but i am pretty sure that they occupy space
on the fileset and we need to account for their extent information as
well. My question was concerns about opening these files and doing a
showfile on them? Hope i have clarified things.

Thanks,
narasimha.

