"Michael K.H. Kim" wrote:
> stack, virtual memory, user memory size etc.  Is there such a
> file?  Could someone
> show me where I can find this?

`sysconfig -q proc` will tell you current limits (default by 
Compaq). You can change them by adding lines in /etc/sysconfigtab, 
eg I had,

proc:
        max_proc_per_user=128
        max_per_proc_stack_size=134217728
        max_per_proc_data_size=8589934592
        max_per_proc_address_space=8589934592
        autonice=1

max_per_proc_data_size/max_per_proc_address_space have a default
up limit of 4GB but we have 8GB memory. If you have 4GB memory +
4GB swap, you may set this limit to 7GB, but that will slow down
everything. 

Check the following sections in the manual for more:

System Configuration and Tuning
5.1    Tuning Process Limits
5.2    Tuning Program Size Limits
5.3    Tuning Address Space Limits

-- 
Cheers,
Ling Shi


